  "method": {
    "collection": "GitHub code search API, five distinct queries (SPEC REPOS, Firebase, EXTERNAL SOURCES, React-Core, CHECKOUT OPTIONS), deduplicated by repository",
    "exposure_rule": "a pod counts as exposed when the lockfile lists it under the central specs index under any spelling (trunk, https://github.com/CocoaPods/Specs, with or without .git); pods pinned via EXTERNAL SOURCES or a private spec repo count as insulated",
    "verification": "counts independently re-derived from the raw lockfiles by a separate script, not by the scanner alone",
    "repository_names_withheld": "deliberately: naming third-party projects as exposed would publish a security posture their owners did not consent to"
  },
  "sampling_caveat": "GitHub code search does not return a random sample. It skews toward smaller, older, public repositories and away from large commercial apps, which are mostly private. These figures describe this corpus; they are not a population estimate for the App Store. n=83 is small and is stated rather than rounded up.",
